%%sep 1 1 500
%%begintext align
%%   The following are a choice Collection of the best original Scotch Dances arranged as Medleys
%% a Strathspey and Reel following alternately in their respective Keys as the frequent changing the Key
%% more or less has been found to offend the Ear.
%%endtext
%%begintext align
%%    The Publishers thought it proper to keep the Slow Tunes by themselves that they might not
%% interrup [sic] the Medleys.
%%endtext
%%begintext align
%% (The first tune (Braes of Tullymet) contains the instructions for playing
%% tunes marked with the "up-arrow + inverted-fermata" symbol, saying that
%% "The Tunes in the Mesley's marked thus may be play Slow when not danced."
%%endtext
% %sep 1 1 500


